# Implementation Plan - Music Distribution Management System

This project is a comprehensive Music Distribution Management System built with **Laravel**. It features a modern, responsive, premium dark-themed interface built using Laravel Blade templates, custom CSS, and custom JavaScript, with no dependencies on complex Node compile pipelines (since Node/npm is not available on the current system). It implements user management, artist verification, release management, simulated store distribution, automated royalty calculations, analytics, and admin monitoring.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Environment Constraints & Technical Choices:**
> 1. **No Node/npm compiler:** As Node.js and npm are not installed, the application will use standard Blade templates combined with custom CSS/JS assets placed directly in `public/` and loaded via standard Laravel asset paths.
> 2. **Database:** The project will be configured to support **SQLite** by default (which requires zero setup and works out of the box), with support for **MySQL** if configured in `.env`.
> 3. **Asset Delivery:** We will use Google Fonts (Outfit / Inter) and FontAwesome (via CDN) for modern premium look and icons. Charts will be drawn using Chart.js (via CDN).

## Proposed Changes

We will create a brand new Laravel application in `c:\wamp64\www\College-Music`.

### Component 1: Project Initialization & Configuration

* **`composer create-project laravel/laravel .`**: Run this command to initialize a new Laravel 11/12 project.
* **`.env`**: Configure database settings to use SQLite (creating `database/database.sqlite`), set the app name to "College Music", and enable file storage links.

### Component 2: Database Schema & Migrations

We will create the following migrations to build our schema:

1. **`create_users_table`**: Extend standard users with `role` (admin, distributor, record_label, artist), `phone`, `status` (active, suspended, deactivated), `verification_code`, `notification_preferences` (JSON), and `email_verified_at`/`phone_verified_at`.
2. **`create_artists_table`**: `id`, `user_id` (nullable), `name`, `bio`, `profile_picture`, `social_links` (JSON), `contact_info`, `verification_status` (pending, verified, rejected), `verification_documents` (JSON/string).
3. **`create_releases_table`**: `id`, `artist_id`, `title`, `type` (single, album, ep), `cover_image`, `genre`, `language`, `release_date`, `copyright_info`, `scheduling_type` (immediate, scheduled), `distribution_status` (pending, approved, distributed, rejected), `rejection_reason`, `billing_status` (unpaid, paid), `price_paid`.
4. **`create_tracks_table`**: `id`, `release_id`, `title`, `artist_name`, `composer`, `songwriter`, `isrc`, `audio_file`, `duration` (seconds).
5. **`create_release_store_table`**: Pivot/linking table tracking store distributions (Spotify, Apple Music, YouTube Music, Deezer, etc.) with distribution status.
6. **`create_royalties_table`**: `id`, `track_id`, `platform`, `amount`, `country`, `date` (YYYY-MM), `streams_count`.
7. **`create_withdrawals_table`**: `id`, `user_id`, `amount`, `payment_method`, `payment_details`, `status` (pending, completed, rejected), `rejection_reason`, `invoice_number`.
8. **`create_subscriptions_table`**: `id`, `user_id`, `plan_name` (Free, Premium), `price`, `status` (active, expired), `starts_at`, `ends_at`.
9. **`create_payments_table`**: `id`, `user_id`, `release_id` (nullable), `subscription_id` (nullable), `amount`, `status` (completed, pending, failed), `payment_method`, `transaction_reference`, `invoice_number`.
10. **`create_audit_logs_table`**: `id`, `user_id` (nullable), `action`, `description`, `ip_address`, `user_agent`.

### Component 3: Models & Relationships

Create the following models:
* `User`: HasOne `Artist` (or HasMany if record label), HasMany `Withdrawals`, HasMany `Payments`, HasOne `Subscription`.
* `Artist`: BelongsTo `User`, HasMany `Releases`.
* `Release`: BelongsTo `Artist`, HasMany `Tracks`, HasMany `ReleaseStores`, HasMany `Payments`.
* `Track`: BelongsTo `Release`, HasMany `Royalties`.
* `ReleaseStore`: BelongsTo `Release`.
* `Royalty`: BelongsTo `Track`.
* `Withdrawal`: BelongsTo `User`.
* `Subscription`: BelongsTo `User`.
* `Payment`: BelongsTo `User`, BelongsTo `Release` (nullable), BelongsTo `Subscription` (nullable).
* `AuditLog`: BelongsTo `User`.

### Component 4: Controllers & Business Logic

* **`AuthController`**: Handles unique email/phone registration, verification link/code flow (simulated screen or mail), login (email or phone), password recovery (verification code entry), log out.
* **`ProfileController` & `SettingsController`**: Edit personal information, upload profile picture, change password, update notification preferences, deactivate account.
* **`ArtistController`**: Artist verification submission (files/IDs), profile bio editing, music catalogue view.
* **`ReleaseController`**: Upload wizard (upload audio files, upload cover image, validate types/sizes, fill metadata, select stores, release scheduling, edit release, request takedown).
* **`DashboardController`**: Aggregates dashboard views (Artist, Record Label, Admin) with earnings stats, streams, top-performing tracks, and notifications.
* **`AnalyticsController`**: Handles streaming analytics, downloads, listener geography charts, monthly/yearly PDF/HTML reports.
* **`PaymentController`**: Handles release payment fees, subscriptions, simulated card checkout, invoice generation and view.
* **`AdminController`**: Management of users (activate/suspend), verification reviews, release reviews (approve/reject with reason), payment reviews (approve withdrawals), system-wide reports, audit log viewer.
* **`SearchController`**: Public or dashboard search engine with filters (genre, country, date, artist).

### Component 5: Premium UI Views (Blade + Custom CSS)

We will build a high-fidelity, visual-first UI layout using standard Tailwind/Bootstrap-inspired responsive grids built entirely in custom CSS, avoiding the lack of build steps:
* **`layouts/app.blade.php`**: The main layout. Dark mode primary background (`#0b0f19`), side navigation, navbar, notifications dropdown, and core script wrappers.
* **`auth/...`**: Login, register (incorporating Artist/Distributor/Record Label choices), verify, and recovery views.
* **`dashboard.blade.php`**: Overview dashboard showing cards with gradient overlays, a glowing Chart.js line graph for streams/earnings, recent releases, and notifications.
* **`releases/create.blade.php`**: Step-by-step release distribution wizard.
* **`releases/show.blade.php`**: Release details page with tracks list, distribution store list, and takedown request option.
* **`analytics/index.blade.php`**: Interactive analytics charts and maps.
* **`finance/index.blade.php`**: Earnings breakdown, payment tables, withdrawal requests, invoice views.
* **`admin/...`**: Admin panels for catalog reviews, withdrawal processing, user suspensions, and audit logs.

